# Plan: Default ActionBar Toggle Options to Off

## Problem
In `ActionBar.tsx`, the 3-dot menu contains toggle options for upcoming features (Pomodoro Timer, Break Timer, Meeting Timer). Currently these default to **ON** (visible) because `hiddenButtons` initializes as an empty object.

## Goal
Make these toggle options default to **OFF** (hidden) so the buttons don't appear in the ActionBar until users explicitly enable them.

## Solution
Set default values for the toggle targets in the initial state.

## File to Modify
- `frontend/src/components/actionbar/ActionBar.tsx`

## Changes

### 1. Create default hidden state constant
Add a constant that sets all TOGGLE_TARGETS to hidden by default:

```tsx
const DEFAULT_HIDDEN: HiddenButtons = {
  pomodoro: true,
  break: true,
  meeting: true,
};
```

### 2. Update initial useState
Change from:
```tsx
const [hiddenButtons, setHiddenButtons] = useState<HiddenButtons>({});
```
To:
```tsx
const [hiddenButtons, setHiddenButtons] = useState<HiddenButtons>(DEFAULT_HIDDEN);
```

### 3. Merge localStorage with defaults in useEffect
Update the useEffect to merge stored preferences over defaults:
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (typeof window === 'undefined') return;
  try {
    const raw = window.localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);
    if (!raw) return;
    const parsed = JSON.parse(raw);
    if (parsed && typeof parsed === 'object') {
      setHiddenButtons({ ...DEFAULT_HIDDEN, ...parsed });
    }
  } catch {
    // ignore malformed storage
  }
}, []);
```

This ensures:
- Fresh users see buttons hidden by default
- Existing users' explicit preferences are preserved
- Any new toggle targets added later will also default to hidden
